cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, cite this release. For the investigation findings, cite the related preprint listed below."
title: "UNK_DeadDrop Companion"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Krasnjanski
    given-names: Ilja
    affiliation: Independent researcher
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-1039-5930"
version: 2.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-28
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/KrasForge/unk-deaddrop-companion"
abstract: "Defensive research companion for the UNK_DeadDrop artifact study. Includes a parse-only JavaScript AST scanner distributed through npm and PyPI, inert boundary fixtures, and 33 experimental YARA file-content rules in 28 files. Every YARA rule matched retained case artifacts in a read-only replay; a small local software baseline produced no hits. Authentic endpoint logs were unavailable, so Sigma event rules are not included. The available corpus does not establish production precision or recall, execution, collection, attribution, or current infrastructure status."
keywords:
  - malware analysis
  - detection engineering
  - static analysis
  - YARA
references:
  - type: preprint
    authors:
      - family-names: Krasnjanski
        given-names: Ilja
    title: "UNK_DeadDrop: An Artifact-Based Study of Recruitment Malware, Credential Collection, and Operator Infrastructure"
    year: 2026
    doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23696198"
    url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23696198"
